{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SplayTree","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A splay tree keeps no balance information. Any sequence of ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" insertions, removals and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accesses on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" elements costs O((","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") log ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") in all, so each takes O(log ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"amortized, and recently or frequently accessed elements stay near the root: accessing the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements in ascending order costs O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") in all. Reads (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"text":", the bounds, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subscripts and iteration) leave the tree as it is, so they keep the value semantics and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API of the other sorted sets, and take time proportional to the element’s depth, which a run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ascending insertions can make ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". Use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/access(_:)"},{"text":" to look an element up and splay it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root","recent.contains(25)           \/\/ false, and the tree is unchanged","let parts = recent.split(at: 30)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [10, 20]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [30, 40, 50]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank like an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array: ","type":"text"},{"code":"tree[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the smallest element. The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"links, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"A sorted set kept in a splay tree: a binary search tree that rotates each element it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accesses, inserts or removes up to the root (Sleator and Tarjan, 1985).","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/docum